  "rules": {
    "phone_price_feature_matrix_v1": "Compare the complete frozen product bodies for price, review display, condition wording, storage and memory, display, camera and video features, network and carrier wording, operating system, battery wording, dimensions, weight, and included adapter or charger language. The Redmi body states $300, 73/100 over 12 reviews, 128 GB and 6 GB RAM in the title, a 6.7-inch AMOLED 120 Hz display, Snapdragon 732G, stereo speakers, four rear cameras, GSM-only and not Verizon or Sprint wording, Android 11, and an adapter or fast charger in the box. The S21 body states $590.01, 62/100 over 12 reviews, factory-unlocked US 5G wording, 128 GB, 8K video, a 64 MP camera, 30 Space Zoom, and a conditional all-day battery statement, but does not state software-support duration or included charger contents. Preserve the $290.01 price difference and do not repair suspicious dimensions or other listing fields from outside knowledge.",
    "battery_longevity_scope_v1": "Treat both product battery descriptions as seller claims, not longitudinal aging tests. Generic lithium-ion evidence says cell life can vary materially with materials and identifies a broad cycle-durability range, but neither product body supplies cell construction, controlled cycle retention, heat exposure, or a matched aging test. The charging thread contains one Redmi Note 10 Pro owner's six-month degradation report and opinions linking fast charging and heat, while the battery-replacement thread contains varied iPhone owner experiences. These anecdotes motivate caution but cannot establish causality, transfer a lifetime, or prove that either price tier ages better.",
    "charging_compatibility_boundary_v1": "USB-C identifies a connector form rather than a guaranteed protocol, Power Delivery implementation, cable capability, or charging wattage. Generic charger evidence says charging voltage, current, completion behavior, and temperature control depend on the battery and charging protocol. The Redmi body explicitly names an included adapter and fast charger. The S21 body does not establish box charger contents. A separate $13.99 no-review seller listing claims a 25 W PD charger and USB-C-to-USB-C cable compatible with S21, but this is seller compatibility wording rather than independent performance or safety validation. Inspect the old charger's connector, cable, output label, condition, and device protocol before reusing it.",
    "support_repairability_boundary_v1": "A different-model Nokia G22 discussion pairs easy battery replacement with complaints about only three years of security updates. It shows that repairability and software support are separate longevity dimensions, but neither the G22 numbers nor its quality judgments transfer to Redmi or S21. Because neither candidate body states update duration, battery replacement cost, or repairability, the snapshot cannot award a longevity advantage to either model on those dimensions. Obtain written model-specific support and service terms before a long-horizon purchase.",
    "evidence_bounded_phone_decision_v1": "For this buyer's stated ordinary use and tight budget, choose the Redmi Note 10 Pro value route if a real carrier and band check plus written update-support check pass. Its frozen listing saves $290.01, supplies 128 GB and 6 GB RAM, a 120 Hz AMOLED display, stereo speakers, four rear cameras, and an included adapter or fast charger, while the buyer does not prioritize the S21's documented 5G, 8K, 64 MP, or 30 Space Zoom features. Preserve the Redmi's international GSM-only limitation, 73/100 over only 12 reviews, seller-only battery wording, charging anecdote, and absent product-specific aging and support evidence. Do not add a charger unless the included adapter is missing, damaged, or incompatible. Select the S21 only if its US 5G and camera features justify the premium after verifying box contents and charging requirements. Defer if carrier compatibility or written support terms cannot be confirmed."
